          "الذين share one parent with the deceased or with each other, contextually half-sisters here as they are excluded by the daughter in this specific ruling context or referring to sisters of the deceased who are daughters of his father and mother if the deceased was male, but the text says 'sister of his father and mother' meaning the sisters are the daughters of the father and mother of the deceased. Wait, 'أُخْتَهُ لِأَبِيهِ وَأُمِّهِ' usually means 'his sister, [who is] from his father and mother', i.e., a full sister. In Shia fiqh, a daughter excludes a full sister. The text says 'sister of the father and mother' which implies full sister. The ruling is that the daughter takes all, excluding the sister.",
